  "caption": "Quinn booked a five-day trek and trained with flat walks to the café. Then the first big downhill arrived, and the knees were not impressed.\n\nFlat walking builds stamina, but descents load the quads and knees in a different way, day after day, often with a pack on.\n\nA 12-week plan can help: strength twice a week (squats, step-ups, split squats, calf raises) with a weekend walk, then add downhills, step-downs and a light pack, then back-to-back days in your real boots and socks. Treat hot spots early, use poles downhill, and taper the final week.\n\nKnown knee, hip or back issue? Get a plan early. Heading to altitude? See a travel doctor.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
